.TH RLOCATE 1 "2026-10-20" "rlocate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rlocate \- find files by name using a trigram index
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rlocate
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fIPATTERN\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rlocate
searches a prebuilt index (see
.BR rlocate-updatedb (1))
for file names matching one or more patterns, printing one match per line.
.PP
By default a pattern matches anywhere in the path (substring). A pattern
containing the glob metacharacters
.BR * ", " ? ", or " [
is matched as an anchored
.BR fnmatch (3)
glob in which
.B *
also matches
.BR / .
With
.B \-r
patterns are treated as regular expressions matched anywhere in the path.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-database " \fIPATH\fR"
Use the index at \fIPATH\fR instead of the platform default.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-regexp
Interpret patterns as regular expressions.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-ignore\-case
Match case-insensitively (disables trigram pruning; scans all names).
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-basename
Match only against the final path component.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-wholename
Match against the whole path (the default; overrides \fB\-b\fR).
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-existing
Only print entries that still exist on disk.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-count
Print only the number of matches.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-limit " \fIN\fR"
Stop after \fIN\fR matches (0 means unlimited). Alias: \fB\-n\fR.
.TP
.BR \-0 ", " \-\-null
Separate results with a NUL byte instead of a newline.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-statistics
Print statistics about the index and exit (no pattern required; local only).
.SS Remote queries
.TP
.BR \-\-serve
Run as a query server instead of searching. Loads the index (\fB\-d\fR or the
default) once and serves clients concurrently.
.TP
.BR \-\-listen " \fIADDR\fR"
Address to bind in \fB\-\-serve\fR mode (default \fB127.0.0.1:9999\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-host " \fIADDR\fR"
Query a remote rlocate server at \fIADDR\fR (\fIhost:port\fR) instead of a local
index. The search runs on the server; only matched paths are returned.
.TP
.BR \-\-token " \fITOKEN\fR"
Shared secret. Required by \fB\-\-serve\fR and sent with every \fB\-\-host\fR
query. The transport is unencrypted plain TCP; use a trusted network or an SSH
tunnel.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
At least one match was found (or \fB\-S\fR was used).
.TP
.B 1
No matches.
.TP
.B 2
An error occurred (for example, the index could not be opened).
.SH DEFAULT INDEX
.B /var/lib/rlocate/rlocate.db
on Linux,
.B /var/db/rlocate/rlocate.db
on macOS when run as root; otherwise a per-user cache path.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rlocate-updatedb (1),
.BR locate (1),
.BR plocate (1)
